---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const controls=[['Input','One Unicode-normalized question; 4–120 code points and at most 256 UTF-8 bytes. URLs, files, new lines and additional context are rejected.'],['Human check','Cloudflare Turnstile is verified server-side before any quota or provider work.'],['Anonymous quota','Two runs per 24-hour bucket derived with keyed HMAC from IP plus an HttpOnly device identifier. Raw IPs are not stored by the application.'],['Fleet quota','At most 40 reservations per UTC day. Each request atomically reserves €0.02 before the provider call.'],['Budget','€25 monthly soft stop and €30 hard ceiling. Redis Lua updates reserved and settled amounts atomically, including parallel requests.'],['Provider','Exactly one allowlisted gpt-5.4-nano Responses API call, 700 maximum output tokens, 12-second timeout, no retry or fallback.'],['Output','Strict JSON Schema and runtime validation require 4–8 branches with query, intent, rationale, source type and assumption.'],['Storage','ai-fanout.com stores neither the raw question nor raw provider result. Operational records contain keyed hashes, versions, token counts, cost, latency and generic status only.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Planner methodology" canonicalPath="/methodology" description="The exact input, model, quota, cost, privacy and evidence contract behind the AI Fanout Planner.">
<header class="page-head"><h1>Planner methodology</h1><div class="page-head-copy"><p>A deliberately bounded planning call whose inputs, output shape, quotas, costs and limits can be inspected.</p><p class="meta-line">Planner 1.0.0 · method 1.0 · owner Matthias Ramahi</p></div></header>
<div class="document-layout"><aside class="document-aside"><dl><div><dt>State</dt><dd>Release candidate, endpoint closed</dd></div><div><dt>Model</dt><dd>gpt-5.4-nano</dd></div><div><dt>Output cap</dt><dd>700 tokens</dd></div><div><dt>Timeout</dt><dd>12 seconds</dd></div></dl></aside><article class="document-body"><h2>What this planner does</h2><p class="document-intro">It generates plausible ways a researcher, editor or SEO practitioner might decompose one question. The branches are hypotheses created by our own planner. They are not actual or recovered Google queries, ChatGPT subqueries, retrieval traces, system prompts or chain of thought.</p><ol class="controls">{controls.map(([title,copy],index)=><li><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div></li>)}</ol><section><h2>How to use the result</h2><p>Treat each branch as a candidate for research, not an instruction to publish. Check demand, overlap, evidence availability, risk and whether an existing page already satisfies the intent. A useful outcome may be a new page, a section, consolidation or no action.</p></section><section><h2>Responsibility and review</h2><p>Matthias Ramahi is Research Owner and operator. He owns planner-version changes, correction decisions, reviewer assignment and the monthly cost envelope. Outputs are not independently reviewed by default. Any published example must identify its date, exact input, model ID, planner version, review status and cost boundary.</p></section><section><h2>Known limits</h2><p>The model can miss an important branch, duplicate an intent, introduce an unsupported assumption or phrase a branch poorly. A fanout is not search-volume evidence, a ranking forecast, an independent provider benchmark or proof that another system used the same path.</p></section><p><a href="/research/methodology">Read the separate Evidence Lab observation methodology</a>.</p></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.document-body>h2{margin:0;font:720 clamp(3rem,6vw,6rem)/.92 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.06em}.controls{margin:3rem 0 5rem;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);list-style:none}.controls li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:4rem 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:1.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--fine-rule)}.controls li>span{color:var(--source);font:1rem/1 var(--font-display)}.controls h3{margin:0;font-size:1rem}.controls p,.document-body section p{max-width:65ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65}.document-body section{margin-top:4rem;padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}.document-body section h2{font:700 clamp(2rem,4vw,3.6rem)/1 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.045em}</style>
